    },
    "q-99412": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99412",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2+\\text{i} \\\\ 1-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the vector $v$ and the rotation-scaling matrix $C$ shown above. Given that $v$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3-2\\text{i},$ find a matrix $P$ such that $A=PC{P}^{-1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nFirst, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\ne C,\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda }) & \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{\\lambda })\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]=C.\n$$\n\nSo, our rotation-scaling matrix $C$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\overset{―}{\\lambda }=3+2\\text{i},$ \n the complex conjugate of $\\lambda .$ Hence, to construct the matrix $P,$ we use the eigenvector $\\overset{―}{v},$ the complex conjugate of $v.$\n\nNext, we find the real and imaginary parts of our eigenvector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{v} & =[\\begin{aligned}2-\\text{i} \\\\ 1+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v})}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now construct $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(\\overset{―}{v}) & \\text{Im}(\\overset{―}{v}) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
