    },
    "q-39166": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39166",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above.\nGiven that $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where $C$ is a rotation-scaling matrix, what is the value of \n$\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any $2\\times 2$ real matrix $A$ with complex eigenvalues, we have $A=PC{P}^{-1},$ where \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Re}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Im}(\\lambda ) \\\\ -\\text{Im}(\\lambda ) & \\text{Re}(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to the complex eigenvalue  $\\lambda .$\n\nTo compute the eigenvalues of $A,$ we solve the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 15 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a}=4\\pm 6\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the eigenvalue $\\lambda =4-6\\text{i}.$ We can immediately construct the rotation-scaling matrix:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n$(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.$ \nIn our case, we have $\\,{\\lambda }_{1}=4-6\\text{i},$ and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ 15 & 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4-6\\text{i} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3+6\\text{i} & -3 \\\\ 15 & -3+6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the homogeneous system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(3+6\\text{i}){x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 15{x}_{1}+(-3+6\\text{i}){x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, the system above has a non-trivial solution. This implies that one row is a multiple of another. As a result, we can drop one of the rows and take one of the variables as free. For example, from the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=(1+2\\text{i}){x}_{1}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ (1+2\\text{i}){x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{1}\\in C.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{1}=1$, we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can construct the matrix $P$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ \\text{Re}(v) & \\text{Im}(v) \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}{{c}^{2}+{d}^{2}}=\\frac{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-39166-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{3}{7}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"602\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-39166-b",
